   "key": "§ Architecture decision records > 001 — Sensitive storage falls back, then repairs",
   "hash": "0ef8c0c2d385f526",
   "does": "Claims: with EncryptionManager's key unreachable (before first unlock), whole files (archive sessions, one-shot raw backups) are written plain with .completeFileProtectionUnlessOpen and recorded in PendingEncryptionLedger (.session/.rawBackup); streamed files (raw RR points, workout streams) keep completeUntilFirstUserAuthentication with plain lines, recorded (.rawBackup/.workoutTrack); the archive index is written plain. Repairs at the next launch with the key, and for the two backup stores also on protectedDataDidBecomeAvailable/didBecomeActive (RawRRBackup.repairAfterUnlock): reencryptPendingSessions, RawRRBackup.reencryptPendingBackups, WorkoutTrackBackup.reencryptPendingTracks, SessionArchive.resealPlainIndexIfNeeded; an id leaves the ledger once no plaintext is left. CloudKit uploads fail closed (CloudPayloadCodec.sealForUpload throws encryptionUnavailable, retried later); rebuildable caches (UI state, training metrics, and the UserDefaults Apple Health caches SleepDataCache and BaselineSnapshot sealed with JSONFileSeal.app) skip the write. Only a throwing encrypt() is logged.",
   "entry": null,
