  {
   "key": "§ Architecture decision records > 007 — One app target, one composition root",
   "hash": "bc9af0a33a13bd00",
   "does": "Summary of ADR 007: the iPhone app is one target and module with its layers as directories, the Watch app, unit tests and UI tests are separate targets; services are reached through AppDependencies (WatchDependencies on the Watch) whose overrides let a test substitute any of them; .shared is read only in those two files, enforced by check_no_shared_outside_root.sh; AppDependencies.current has no setter and only a test puts another container in force, for a scope that restores the previous one; the launch work and the data purge are handed exactly the services they use, and check_explicit_dependencies.sh keeps container reads out of them and install out of app code. Consistent with 007-single-target-composition-root.md.",
